course: dictionary
lesson: 4881
title: Words that can hurt
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An idiot is a person who does something very stupid. It is also a name people use to insult someone, and that can hurt their feelings. Read the words around it to see how it is being used.
explain: «You idiot!» shouted at a friend is name-calling, and it is not allowed at school. Sometimes people say «I'm such an idiot» about their own small mistake, like forgetting their PE kit. That is joking about themselves, not an insult to someone else.
explain: Be careful, because idiot is never a kind word for another person. Long ago it was a medical word for someone with a learning disability, but it is offensive now and should not be used that way. Ask yourself: is this word kind or unkind here?
fact: An idiot is a person who does something very stupid.
fact: Calling someone «an idiot» is an insult, and it can hurt their feelings.
fact: People may say «I feel like an idiot» or «I made an idiot of myself» about their own silly mistake.
fact: Other words with the same meaning are «muppet» (UK slang), «numpty» (Scotland) and «eejit» (Northern Ireland).
fact: Long ago, idiot was a medical word for a person with a learning disability, but this use is offensive now.
exercise: «You idiot!» shouted at a friend is what kind of word? | A kind compliment | A medical term used today | A joke about a pet | *Name-calling that can hurt feelings
exercise: Sam says, «I'm such an idiot, I left my lunch at home.» What is Sam doing? | Telling a story about a dog | Insulting a teacher | *Laughing at his own small mistake | Giving a medical report
exercise: Which slang word from Northern Ireland means idiot? | Servo | Dreich | Nah yeah | *Eejit
test: Why is it unkind to call a classmate «an idiot»? | It is a medical word used today | It is a compliment | *It is an insult that can hurt their feelings | It means they are very clever
test: Long ago, idiot was a medical word for what? | A broken bone | *A person with a learning disability | A kind of pet food | A type of cloud
exam: Which sentence uses idiot as an insult to another person? | «I made an idiot of myself at the party» | «I'm such an idiot for forgetting my book» | «Look at the cloud shaped like a dog» | *«You idiot, get out of my way!»
